From 0c64604056c2171d2c70ad9f8d9928cf4e61d1b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorik Dalloshi <lorik@Loriks-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:45:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(macos): verified writes, window pinning, paste entry
 and diff read-back

Rebased onto upstream v1.1.5 (6a49b44); upstream semantics win where they
overlap:

- set_value: upstream's exact read-back (#111) is the final check and
  password fields are never read (#164). Added on top: text fields inside
  web content are filled with real keystrokes so frameworks such as React
  register the edit, a native text field that ignores the AX write is
  retried with keystrokes, and a write that left the field unchanged says
  so.
- type_text: upstream's live focus and selection-replacing AX write (#130)
  stay the default path; the fork's append-only AX write is dropped.
  Added on top: the field last clicked stands in when macOS reports no
  focus for a background app, web content gets keystrokes, the field is
  read back and a WARNING returned when it did not change. New method:
  auto | keys | paste (clipboard + Cmd+V, clipboard restored).
  Password fields are never read back (readableValue answers nil).
- get_app_state window_id / window_title pin a window: snapshots, actions
  and read-backs stay on it (#83 finding 1). The header lists the app's
  windows; an action whose read-back lands on another window says so.
- OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_ACTION_RESULT=diff returns only changed tree lines
  when the window is unchanged and few lines moved (#16, #83 finding 6a);
  OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_ACTION_SCREENSHOT=0 skips read-back capture.

Dropped as superseded: the OPEN_COMPUTER_USE_APP_VARIANT=dev build switch
(upstream #141).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
